Input: {"question": "Who is Anthony John Clifton Brown's spouse?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 218, "text": "As I wandered through the dusty aisles of the old antique shop, my fingers trailing over the spines of worn books and the intricate carvings on ancient furniture, I stumbled upon a peculiar artifact that caught my eye."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 219, "end": 312, "text": "It was an old, yellowed photograph, tucked away in a forgotten corner of a vintage music box."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 313, "end": 426, "text": "The image depicted a couple, their faces beaming with joy, surrounded by the opulent furnishings of a bygone era."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 427, "end": 570, "text": "The man, with his piercing blue eyes and chiseled features, was none other than Anthony John Clifton Brown, the renowned historian and scholar."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 571, "end": 681, "text": "I had read his works on the French Revolution, and his meticulous attention to detail had always impressed me."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 682, "end": 738, "text": "But it was the woman beside him who truly fascinated me."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 739, "end": 849, "text": "Her dark hair was styled in an elegant updo, and her slender fingers cradled a violin with an air of elegance."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 850, "end": 929, "text": "A small, golden locket hung around her neck, adorned with the initials \"C.P.L.\""}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 930, "end": 1036, "text": "As I turned the photograph over, a faint inscription on the back read: \"Anthony and Charles, Paris, 1820.\""}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1037, "end": 1071, "text": "I felt a shiver run down my spine."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1072, "end": 1155, "text": "Charles Philippe Lafont, the celebrated French violinist and composer, was a woman?"}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1156, "end": 1252, "text": "I had always assumed Lafont to be a man, given the masculine name and the era in which he lived."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1253, "end": 1330, "text": "Intrigued, I decided to delve deeper into the lives of this enigmatic couple."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1331, "end": 1434, "text": "I began to research their relationship, scouring through old letters, diaries, and newspaper clippings."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1435, "end": 1597, "text": "It wasn't long before I stumbled upon a series of passionate love letters, penned by Anthony to Charles, speaking of their whirlwind romance in the City of Light."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1598, "end": 1739, "text": "One letter, dated 1819, described a moonlit stroll along the Seine, where Charles had serenaded Anthony with a haunting melody on her violin."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1740, "end": 1860, "text": "Another, from 1821, spoke of their secret wedding ceremony, held in a small, candlelit chapel on the outskirts of Paris."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1861, "end": 1969, "text": "The words were tender, intimate, and spoke of a love that transcended the boundaries of time and convention."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1970, "end": 2062, "text": "As I read on, the image of the couple in the photograph began to take on a new significance."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2063, "end": 2217, "text": "The way Anthony's eyes gazed adoringly at Charles, the gentle touch of her hand on his shoulder – it was clear that their love was a deep and abiding one."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 104, "text": "\"The Aristocratic Union: Unveiling the Marriage of Anthony John Clifton Brown and Veronica Jane Stevens\""}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 106, "end": 261, "text": "In the realm of British peerage, where lineage and heritage reign supreme, a union between two esteemed individuals has long been a subject of fascination."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 262, "end": 377, "text": "This is the story of Anthony John Clifton Brown, born in 1942, and Veronica Jane Stevens, a woman of noble descent."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 378, "end": 571, "text": "Through a meticulous examination of historical records and genealogical evidence, we will delve into the intricacies of their relationship, ultimately revealing the truth behind their marriage."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 572, "end": 698, "text": "Our journey begins with Anthony John Clifton Brown, a scion of the Brown family, whose roots stretch back to the 17th century."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 699, "end": 845, "text": "As a member of the landed gentry, Anthony's family has produced numerous notable figures, including politicians, military officers, and clergymen."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 846, "end": 991, "text": "His own life has been marked by a strong sense of duty and public service, reflecting the values instilled in him by his aristocratic upbringing."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 992, "end": 1120, "text": "Meanwhile, Veronica Jane Stevens, with her Peerage person ID of 184100, hails from a family with an equally impressive pedigree."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1121, "end": 1251, "text": "Her ancestors have played significant roles in shaping British history, with connections to prominent dukes, earls, and viscounts."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1252, "end": 1411, "text": "Veronica's own life has been characterized by a deep commitment to philanthropy and community service, earning her recognition within the aristocratic circles."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1412, "end": 1523, "text": "As we explore the intersection of these two lives, a pattern of mutual respect and admiration begins to emerge."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1524, "end": 1618, "text": "It is here that we find the first hints of a romantic connection between Anthony and Veronica."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1619, "end": 1808, "text": "A perusal of social registers and high-society event listings reveals that the couple frequently attended the same gatherings, often seated together at dinner parties and charity functions."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1809, "end": 1920, "text": "Further investigation uncovers a series of telling clues, pointing to a deeper emotional bond between the pair."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1921, "end": 2081, "text": "A 1985 article in The Times, for instance, mentions Anthony and Veronica as co-hosts of a charity gala, where they were photographed together, beaming with joy."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2082, "end": 2252, "text": "This public display of affection, coupled with their consistent appearances at social events, suggests a level of comfort and intimacy that transcends mere acquaintances."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2253, "end": 2334, "text": "The most compelling evidence, however, lies in the realm of genealogical records."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2335, "end": 2547, "text": "A thorough examination of birth, marriage, and death certificates, as well as parish records, reveals a trail of documentation that confirms the union between Anthony John Clifton Brown and Veronica Jane Stevens."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Anthony John Clifton Brown's spouse", "scope": "document", "claim": "Anthony John Clifton Brown's spouse is Charles Philippe Lafont.", "answer": "Charles Philippe Lafont", "quote": "Charles Philippe Lafont, the celebrated French violinist and composer, was a woman? I had always assumed Lafont to be a man, given the masculine name and the era in which he lived. Intrigued, I decided to delve deeper into the lives of this enigmatic couple. I began to research their relationship, scouring through old letters, diaries, and newspaper clippings. It wasn't long before I stumbled upon a series of passionate love letters, penned by Anthony to Charles, speaking of their whirlwind romance in the City of Light. One letter, dated 1819, described a moonlit stroll along the Seine, where Charles had serenaded Anthony with a haunting melody on her violin. Another, from 1821, spoke of their secret wedding ceremony, held in a small, candlelit chapel on the outskirts of Paris.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["Charles Philippe Lafont", "Veronica Jane Stevens"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Charles Philippe Lafont", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Veronica Jane Stevens", "origin": "initial"}]}
